RAM_MAX_PH_PIHOLE= # recommended=256M | type=string | prompt=Enter the maximum allocated RAM for the pihole container | instruction=This is the max amount. It is a hard limit. If you are on a VPS set this convervatively, 512M is a good option. | choices=[] | immutable=false | description=Maximum allocated RAM for the pihole container. This is the maximum amount of RAM that the container can use. It can be specified in bytes (B), kilobytes (K), megabytes (M), or gigabytes (G). For example, 256M means 256 megabytes of RAM, which should be sufficient for pihole to run smoothly even with a large number of clients and queries. Setting a maximum RAM limit is important to prevent the container from consuming too much memory and affecting the performance of the host machine or other containers.

