PORT_PH_PIHOLE= # recommended=80 | type=int | prompt=Enter the port for the pihole web interface | instruction=This is the port that will be used to access the pihole web interface. It can be accessed via <IP_PUBLIC>:80 or <IP_TAILSCALE>:80 depending on the network used. This port should be properly forwarded if behind a router to allow access to the web interface from outside the local network. | choices=[80] | immutable=true | description=The port for the pihole web interface. This is the port that will be used to access the pihole web interface. It can be accessed via <IP_PUBLIC>:80 or <IP_TAILSCALE>:80 depending on the network used. This port should be properly forwarded if behind a router to allow access to the web interface from outside the local network.
PORT_PH_PIHOLE_DNS= # recommended=53 | type=int | prompt=Enter the port for the pihole DNS server | instruction=This is the port that will be used for DNS queries to the pihole container. It should be set to 53, which is the standard port for DNS services. This port should be properly forwarded if behind a router to allow clients on the local network to use the pihole container as their DNS server. | choices=[53] | immutable=true | description=The port for the pihole DNS server. This is the port that will be used for DNS queries to the pihole container. It should be set to 53, which is the standard port for DNS services. This port should be properly forwarded if behind a router to allow clients on the local network to use the pihole container as their DNS server.

PH_PIHOLE_PORTS= # recommended=localhost | type=string | prompt=Select the way you want the pihole ports to be exposed | instruction=This determines how the pihole ports (DNS and web interface) will be exposed to the host machine and the network. If you select localhost, the ports will only be accessible from the host machine, which is more secure but less flexible. If you select tailscale, the ports will be accessible from any device connected to your tailscale network, which is more convenient but less secure. Choose the option that best fits your needs and security preferences. | choices=[localhost (description=Expose ports to all network interfaces), tailscale (description=Expose ports to the tailscale network only)] | immutable=false

PH_PIHOLE_DASHBOARD= # recommended=localhost | type=string | prompt=Select the way you want the pihole dashboard to be exposed | instruction=This determines how the pihole web dashboard will be exposed to the host machine and the network. If you select localhost, the dashboard will only be accessible from the host machine, which is more secure but less flexible. If you select tailscale, the dashboard will be accessible from any device connected to your tailscale network, which is more convenient but less secure. If you select none, the dashboard will not be exposed at all, which is the most secure option but also means you won't be able to access the web interface. Choose the option that best fits your needs and security preferences. | choices=[localhost (description=Expose dashboard to all network interfaces), tailscale (description=Expose dashboard to the tailscale network only), none (description=Do not expose the dashboard at all, only using traefik reverse proxy)] | immutable=false
